







LAMPLIGHT

A TXA sample game

A lighthouse gone dark, an old keeper who has lost his spectacles, a tide that will not wait, and a ship that is coming whether the lamp is lit or not.



Press any key to begin.
The wind has turned cold, and out across the bay the lighthouse stands dark against the last of the sunset. It should have been lit an hour ago.

Harbour Road
A cobbled road above the harbour. The keeper's cottage is north, its door ajar; a boat shed stands to the west. The quay is east, and steps lead down to the beach to the south.

>look
Harbour Road
A cobbled road above the harbour. The keeper's cottage is north, its door ajar; a boat shed stands to the west. The quay is east, and steps lead down to the beach to the south.

>n
Cottage Kitchen
A low kitchen warm from the stove. A dresser stands against one wall, and a ladder climbs to the room above.
A storm lantern hangs on a hook by the door.
Old Brannock, the keeper, sits by the stove, squinting at nothing.
On the dresser is a drawer.

>x keeper
White-whiskered and half-blind without his spectacles.

>ask brannock about lamp
"Gone out, has it? I can't climb that stair, not with my eyes. There's oil in the boat shed. Matches in the drawer."

>ask him about key
"The shed key? I've got it somewhere. Find my spectacles and I'll find the key."

>take lantern
Taken.

>open drawer
You open the drawer.

>take matches
Taken.

>u
Loft Bedroom
A narrow loft under the eaves, just room for a bed and a nightstand.
On the nightstand is a pair of spectacles.

>take spectacles
Taken.

>d
Cottage Kitchen
Old Brannock, the keeper, sits by the stove, squinting at nothing.
On the dresser is a drawer.

>give spectacles to brannock
Brannock puts the spectacles on and beams at you. "That's better." He fishes a key from his pocket and presses it into your hand.

