>e
Causeway
Flat stones, slick with weed, with the sea on both sides. The quay is west and the lighthouse rock east.

>e
Lighthouse Rock
Black rock round the foot of the lighthouse, whose door is north. The causeway leads back west.

>n
Lighthouse Base
A round room of whitewashed stone. A spiral stair climbs into darkness; a store room is east, and the door out is south.

>u
Spiral Stair
The iron stair winds up and up. Down is the base; up, the watch room.

>u
Watch Room
The keeper's watch room: a desk under the window, a stool, and the last of the light over the sea. The stair goes down, and a short ladder up to the lamp.
On the desk is a logbook.

>read log
The last entry, in a shaky hand: "Wick trimmed. Oil low - fetch from shed."

>u
Lamp Room
The great lens fills the room, its glass catching what light is left. A door leads out to the gallery.

>x lens
A tower of glass prisms around a wick. The oil reservoir is dry.

>light lens with matches
The wick is dry; it won't take a flame.

>pour oil into lens
You fill the reservoir from the can, and the wick darkens as it drinks.

[Your score has just gone up by 5 points.]

>light lens with matches
You strike a match and touch it to the wick. The flame catches, steadies, and the great lens takes it, throwing a slow beam out across the water. Far out, a ship's horn answers.

*** You have won ***

In that game you scored 25 out of a possible 25, in 47 turns.
